# Graph core

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), the single source of repository instructions.

- Keep graph-core limited to graph/state/node/edge types, schemas, typed validation errors,
  and pure utilities. Rust is the canonical engine model; keep the TypeScript surface aligned.
- No network, filesystem, storage, LLM calls, execution logic, or imports from graph-runtime.
- Graph conditions are named registry predicates, never inline executable expressions.
  Resolution belongs to the runtime.
- Preserve the graph definition's semver `version` field. Schema changes must be compatible
  or introduce a new version; public API changes need maintainer review.
- Expose TypeScript public APIs through the package root. Validate external data with Zod.
